
// Generated by Melissa Bianco's Almighty Fingers ver 69 on Fri Apr 30 2005

// Sharkhead Isle

// HISTORY

// Eldritch War
"CoTHistory4" "Sharkhead Isle was given its name by the free traders who first mapped and settled it in the early 1600s. For many years it served as a hub for the rest of the Isles, with its naturally protected bay as a home port for explorers, entrepreneurs, and pirates. Sharkhead Isle also acted as a central hub for many of the mystics and witchdoctors of the era, who sought the rare shards of red crystal coral. Even in the modern day, would-be practitioners of magic like the cultists of the Circle of Thorns still attempt to illegally acquire shards of Red Coral Crystal, believing in its supernatural power. This had made it necessary for trade in the Red Crystal Coral to be declared illegal. Any shards of Red Coral Crystal must be turned over to Arachnos to prevent this illegal practice from causing trouble again."

// Arachnos Rising
"RecluseHistory2" "Sharkhead Isle was a den of pirates, cutthroats, and thieves during the Golden Age of Piracy. When those days ended, it was abandoned and taken over by wildlife. Lord Recluse brought true prosperity to Sharkhead when bauxite was discovered and the Cage Consortium given the license to exploit it."

// Mako History
"MakoHistory1" "The vigilante known as Scrapyard was brought down by the heroic Captain Mako on this spot."

// TOURISM

// Razor Toothed
"Sharkhead1" "This is the spot where Mako paraded Scrapyard's body after he eviscerated him.  Many of the locals have seen his ghost in this area."

// Forgegd by Hellfire
"Sharkhead2" "The Hell Forge is the largest above-ground furnace on the planet."

// Freak of Nature
"Sharkhead3" "The Freakshow have managed to find utopia in this forsaken slag heap."

// Pit Viper
"Sharkhead4" "This hole is used by the locals as a makeshift arena for fighting and wagering."

